# AI Placement Copilot

A hybrid AI system that answers placement-related questions in natural language by routing between structured database analytics and document retrieval.

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Question] --> B[FastAPI /ask endpoint]
    B --> C{Intent Router}
    C -->|Analytics question| D[Text-to-SQL via Groq]
    D --> E[PostgreSQL]
    E --> H[Final Answer]
    C -->|Policy/document question| F[Sentence-Transformers Embedding]
    F --> G[pgvector Similarity Search]
    G --> I[Groq LLM Generation]
    I --> H
```

## How it works
- **Analytics questions** (e.g. "How many students got placed at Microsoft?") → Groq converts natural language to SQL → executed against PostgreSQL → returns structured answer.
- **Policy/document questions** → question is embedded via Sentence-Transformers (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`) → cosine similarity search against PostgreSQL using `pgvector` (`<=>` operator) → retrieved context passed to Groq for final answer generation.
- **Intent Router** (rule-based) classifies each incoming question and dispatches it to the correct branch.

## Stack
FastAPI · PostgreSQL + pgvector · SQLAlchemy · Sentence-Transformers · Groq LLM · Docker

## Data
Synthetic placement dataset generated via Faker — no real student data used.

## Status
- ✅ SQL analytics branch (Text-to-SQL via Groq, `/ask` endpoint)
- ✅ RAG branch (embeddings + pgvector retrieval)
- ✅ Intent router combining both branches
- 🔧 Frontend — in progress
